  <\notes-news-item>
    <with|font-series|bold|<hlink|Non-commutative <specific|texmacs|<verbatim|L^{p}>><specific|html*|\\(L^{p}\\)> spaces and Grassmann stochastic analysis|paper/noncommutative-lp-grassmann/>>

    By Francesco C. De Vecchi, Luca Fresta, Maria Gordina and Massimiliano Gubinelli.

    <hlink|HTML|site/noncommutative-lp-grassmann/noncommutative-lp-grassmann.html> \<cdot\> <hlink|PDF|ocfl/noncommutative-lp-grassmann/v1/content/paper.pdf> \<cdot\> <specific|texmacs|<hlink|TeXmacs source|ocfl/noncommutative-lp-grassmann/v1/content/source/grassmann-lp-arXiv.tm>><specific|html*|<hlink|TeXmacs source|ocfl/noncommutative-lp-grassmann/v1/content/source/grassmann-lp-arXiv.texmacs>> \<cdot\> <hlink|arXiv:2305.08497|https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.08497>

    <specific|texmacs|<\folded>
      Abstract
    <|folded>
        We introduce a theory of non-commutative <specific|texmacs|<verbatim|L^{p}>><specific|html*|\\(L^{p}\\)> spaces suitable for non-commutative probability in a non-tracial setting and use it to develop stochastic analysis of Grassmann-valued processes, including martingale inequalities, stochastic integrals with respect to Grassmann Itô processes, Girsanov's formula and a weak formulation of Grassmann SDEs. We apply this new setting to the construction of several unbounded random variables including a Grassmann analog of the <specific|texmacs|<verbatim|\\Phi^{4}_{2}>><specific|html*|\\(\\Phi^{4}_{2}\\)> Euclidean QFT in a bounded region and weak solution to singular SPDEs in the spirit of the early work of Jona-Lasinio and Mitter on the stochastic quantisation of <specific|texmacs|<verbatim|\\Phi^{4}_{2}>><specific|html*|\\(\\Phi^{4}_{2}\\)>.
    </folded>><specific|html*|<html-tag|details|<html-tag|summary|Abstract><\html-div-class|paper-abstract>
        We introduce a theory of non-commutative <specific|texmacs|<verbatim|L^{p}>><specific|html*|\\(L^{p}\\)> spaces suitable for non-commutative probability in a non-tracial setting and use it to develop stochastic analysis of Grassmann-valued processes, including martingale inequalities, stochastic integrals with respect to Grassmann Itô processes, Girsanov's formula and a weak formulation of Grassmann SDEs. We apply this new setting to the construction of several unbounded random variables including a Grassmann analog of the <specific|texmacs|<verbatim|\\Phi^{4}_{2}>><specific|html*|\\(\\Phi^{4}_{2}\\)> Euclidean QFT in a bounded region and weak solution to singular SPDEs in the spirit of the early work of Jona-Lasinio and Mitter on the stochastic quantisation of <specific|texmacs|<verbatim|\\Phi^{4}_{2}>><specific|html*|\\(\\Phi^{4}_{2}\\)>.
    </html-div-class>>>

