  <\notes-news-item>
    <with|font-series|bold|<hlink|The <specific|texmacs|<verbatim|\\Phi^4_3>><specific|html*|\\(\\Phi^4_3\\)> measure via Girsanov's theorem|paper/phi43-girsanov/>>

    By Nikolay Barashkov and Massimiliano Gubinelli.

    <hlink|HTML|site/phi43-girsanov/phi43-girsanov.html> \<cdot\> <hlink|PDF|ocfl/phi43-girsanov/v2/content/paper.pdf> \<cdot\> <specific|texmacs|<hlink|TeXmacs source|ocfl/phi43-girsanov/v2/content/texmacs/girsanov-phi43-3.tm>><specific|html*|<hlink|TeXmacs source|ocfl/phi43-girsanov/v2/content/texmacs/girsanov-phi43-3.texmacs>> \<cdot\> <hlink|arXiv:2004.01513|https://arxiv.org/abs/2004.01513>

    <specific|texmacs|<\folded>
      Abstract
    <|folded>
        We construct the <specific|texmacs|<verbatim|\\Phi^4_3>><specific|html*|\\(\\Phi^4_3\\)> measure on a periodic three dimensional box as an absolutely continuous perturbation of a random shift of the Gaussian free field. The shifted measure is constructed via Girsanov's theorem and the relevant filtration is the one generated by a scale parameter. As a byproduct we give a self-contained proof that the <specific|texmacs|<verbatim|\\Phi^4_3>><specific|html*|\\(\\Phi^4_3\\)> measure is singular wrt. the Gaussian free field.
    </folded>><specific|html*|<html-tag|details|<html-tag|summary|Abstract><\html-div-class|paper-abstract>
        We construct the <specific|texmacs|<verbatim|\\Phi^4_3>><specific|html*|\\(\\Phi^4_3\\)> measure on a periodic three dimensional box as an absolutely continuous perturbation of a random shift of the Gaussian free field. The shifted measure is constructed via Girsanov's theorem and the relevant filtration is the one generated by a scale parameter. As a byproduct we give a self-contained proof that the <specific|texmacs|<verbatim|\\Phi^4_3>><specific|html*|\\(\\Phi^4_3\\)> measure is singular wrt. the Gaussian free field.
    </html-div-class>>>

