  <\notes-news-item>
    <with|font-series|bold|<hlink|Global solutions to elliptic and parabolic <specific|texmacs|<verbatim|\\Phi^4>><specific|html*|\\(\\Phi^4\\)> models in Euclidean space|paper/phi4-global-solutions/>>

    By Massimiliano Gubinelli and Martina Hofmanová.

    <hlink|PDF|ocfl/phi4-global-solutions/v2/content/paper.pdf> \<cdot\> <hlink|LaTeX source|ocfl/phi4-global-solutions/v2/content/source/elliptic_phi45-final.tex> \<cdot\> <hlink|arXiv:1804.11253|https://arxiv.org/abs/1804.11253>

    <specific|texmacs|<\folded>
      Abstract
    <|folded>
        We prove existence of global solutions to singular SPDEs on <specific|texmacs|<verbatim|\\mathbb{R}^d>><specific|html*|\\(\\mathbb{R}^d\\)> with cubic nonlinearities and additive white noise perturbation, both in the elliptic setting in dimensions <specific|texmacs|<verbatim|d=4,5>><specific|html*|\\(d=4,5\\)> and in the parabolic setting for <specific|texmacs|<verbatim|d=2,3>><specific|html*|\\(d=2,3\\)>. We prove uniqueness and coming down from infinity for the parabolic equations. A motivation for considering these equations is the construction of scalar interacting Euclidean quantum field theories. The parabolic equations are related to the <specific|texmacs|<verbatim|\\Phi^4_d>><specific|html*|\\(\\Phi^4_d\\)> Euclidean quantum field theory via Parisi\<#2013\>Wu stochastic quantization, while the elliptic equations are linked to the <specific|texmacs|<verbatim|\\Phi^4_{d-2}>><specific|html*|\\(\\Phi^4_{d-2}\\)> Euclidean quantum field theory via the Parisi\<#2013\>Sourlas dimensional reduction mechanism.
    </folded>><specific|html*|<html-tag|details|<html-tag|summary|Abstract><\html-div-class|paper-abstract>
        We prove existence of global solutions to singular SPDEs on <specific|texmacs|<verbatim|\\mathbb{R}^d>><specific|html*|\\(\\mathbb{R}^d\\)> with cubic nonlinearities and additive white noise perturbation, both in the elliptic setting in dimensions <specific|texmacs|<verbatim|d=4,5>><specific|html*|\\(d=4,5\\)> and in the parabolic setting for <specific|texmacs|<verbatim|d=2,3>><specific|html*|\\(d=2,3\\)>. We prove uniqueness and coming down from infinity for the parabolic equations. A motivation for considering these equations is the construction of scalar interacting Euclidean quantum field theories. The parabolic equations are related to the <specific|texmacs|<verbatim|\\Phi^4_d>><specific|html*|\\(\\Phi^4_d\\)> Euclidean quantum field theory via Parisi\<#2013\>Wu stochastic quantization, while the elliptic equations are linked to the <specific|texmacs|<verbatim|\\Phi^4_{d-2}>><specific|html*|\\(\\Phi^4_{d-2}\\)> Euclidean quantum field theory via the Parisi\<#2013\>Sourlas dimensional reduction mechanism.
    </html-div-class>>>

