    <hlink|<verbatim|1595a28d72d19008ef4093777c8375c0...>|ocfl/phi4-global-solutions/v3/inventory.json>>
  </notes-news-item>

  <\notes-news-item>
    <with|font-series|bold|<hlink|Weak universality for a class of 3d stochastic reaction-diffusion models|paper/phi43-weak-universality/>>

    By Marco Furlan and Massimiliano Gubinelli.

    <hlink|HTML|site/phi43-weak-universality/phi43-weak-universality.html> \<cdot\> <hlink|PDF|ocfl/phi43-weak-universality/v3/content/paper.pdf> \<cdot\> <specific|texmacs|<hlink|TeXmacs source|ocfl/phi43-weak-universality/v3/content/texmacs/weak_phi4_PTRF_revised.tm>><specific|html*|<hlink|TeXmacs source|ocfl/phi43-weak-universality/v3/content/texmacs/weak_phi4_PTRF_revised.texmacs>> \<cdot\> <hlink|arXiv:1708.03118|https://arxiv.org/abs/1708.03118>

    <specific|texmacs|<\folded>
      Abstract
    <|folded>
        We establish the large scale convergence of a class of stochastic weakly nonlinear reaction-diffusion models on a three dimensional periodic domain to the dynamic <specific|texmacs|<verbatim|\\Phi^4_3>><specific|html*|\\(\\Phi^4_3\\)> model within the framework of paracontrolled distributions. Our work extends previous results of Hairer and Xu to nonlinearities with a finite amount of smoothness (in particular <specific|texmacs|<verbatim|C^9>><specific|html*|\\(C^9\\)> is enough). We use the Malliavin calculus to perform a partial chaos expansion of the stochastic terms and control their <specific|texmacs|<verbatim|L^p>><specific|html*|\\(L^p\\)> norms in terms of the graphs of the standard <specific|texmacs|<verbatim|\\Phi^4_3>><specific|html*|\\(\\Phi^4_3\\)> stochastic terms.
    </folded>><specific|html*|<html-tag|details|<html-tag|summary|Abstract><\html-div-class|paper-abstract>
        We establish the large scale convergence of a class of stochastic weakly nonlinear reaction-diffusion models on a three dimensional periodic domain to the dynamic <specific|texmacs|<verbatim|\\Phi^4_3>><specific|html*|\\(\\Phi^4_3\\)> model within the framework of paracontrolled distributions. Our work extends previous results of Hairer and Xu to nonlinearities with a finite amount of smoothness (in particular <specific|texmacs|<verbatim|C^9>><specific|html*|\\(C^9\\)> is enough). We use the Malliavin calculus to perform a partial chaos expansion of the stochastic terms and control their <specific|texmacs|<verbatim|L^p>><specific|html*|\\(L^p\\)> norms in terms of the graphs of the standard <specific|texmacs|<verbatim|\\Phi^4_3>><specific|html*|\\(\\Phi^4_3\\)> stochastic terms.
    </html-div-class>>>

