  <\notes-news-item>
    <with|font-series|bold|<hlink|Renormalization of the two-dimensional stochastic nonlinear wave equations|paper/stochastic-wave-2d/>>

    By Massimiliano Gubinelli, Herbert Koch and Tadahiro Oh.

    <hlink|PDF|ocfl/stochastic-wave-2d/v2/content/paper.pdf> \<cdot\> <hlink|LaTeX source|ocfl/stochastic-wave-2d/v2/content/source/1703.05461.tex> \<cdot\> <hlink|arXiv:1703.05461|https://arxiv.org/abs/1703.05461>

    <specific|texmacs|<\folded>
      Abstract
    <|folded>
        We study the two-dimensional stochastic nonlinear wave equations (SNLW) with an additive space-time white noise forcing. In particular, we introduce a time-dependent renor- malization and prove that SNLW is pathwise locally well-posed. As an application of the local well-posedness argument, we also establish a weak universality result for the renormalized SNLW.
    </folded>><specific|html*|<html-tag|details|<html-tag|summary|Abstract><\html-div-class|paper-abstract>
        We study the two-dimensional stochastic nonlinear wave equations (SNLW) with an additive space-time white noise forcing. In particular, we introduce a time-dependent renor- malization and prove that SNLW is pathwise locally well-posed. As an application of the local well-posedness argument, we also establish a weak universality result for the renormalized SNLW.
    </html-div-class>>>

    <with|font-size|0.84|par-mode|left|first issued 16 March 2017; version 2 (arXiv v2), 23 May 2018<next-line>arXiv comments: 24 pages, Typos corrected. To appear in Trans. Amer. Math. Soc<next-line>pin:
