  <\notes-news-item>
    <with|font-series|bold|<hlink|One-dimensional reflected rough differential equations|paper/reflected-rough-equations/>>

    By Aurelien Deya, Massimiliano Gubinelli, Martina Hofmanova and Samy Tindel.

    <hlink|PDF|ocfl/reflected-rough-equations/v1/content/paper.pdf> \<cdot\> <hlink|LaTeX source|ocfl/reflected-rough-equations/v1/content/source/1610.07481.tex> \<cdot\> <hlink|arXiv:1610.07481|https://arxiv.org/abs/1610.07481>

    <specific|texmacs|<\folded>
      Abstract
    <|folded>
        We prove existence and uniqueness of the solution of a one-dimensional rough differential equation driven by a step-2 rough path and reflected at zero. In order to deal with the lack of control of the reflection measure the proof uses some ideas we introduced in a previous work dealing with rough kinetic PDEs [arXiv:1604.00437].
    </folded>><specific|html*|<html-tag|details|<html-tag|summary|Abstract><\html-div-class|paper-abstract>
        We prove existence and uniqueness of the solution of a one-dimensional rough differential equation driven by a step-2 rough path and reflected at zero. In order to deal with the lack of control of the reflection measure the proof uses some ideas we introduced in a previous work dealing with rough kinetic PDEs [arXiv:1604.00437].
    </html-div-class>>>

